    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "i guess i'm just wondering about the \"measure of success\" part. if the growth mainly benefits capital and leaves everyone else behind, wouldn't a lot of economists argue that isn't actually a \"success\" for the economy as a whole? it feels like you're framing it as if the growth is the only thing that matters.",
